<title>SWITZERLAND: Galileo buys SAirGroup's Traviswiss.</title>
<headline>Galileo buys SAirGroup's Traviswiss.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic reservations company Galileo International Inc has acquired SAirGroup's subsidiary, Traviswiss, Switzerland's leading travel reservation system.</p>
<p>The purchase price amounted to $8.0 million and SAirGroup also earned $108 million through the initial public offering (IPO) of Galileo last week, SAirGroup said in a statement.</p>
<p>SAirGroup said the purchase agreements were signed today.</p>
<p>SairGroup's stake in Galileo was reduced to seven percent from 13.2 percent through the IPO.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
